# The twin of a-name-read-off-what-is-one-literal-or-a-number-asks-the-cell: the same labels, in no loop. A test of the cell with the slot's read behind it and the closed read beside it is bytes for time, and those are spent in loops
# alone: here each label stays the closed read that it was. (Asked everywhere, the second try at every such read also cost the build of a large program 0.22 G for nothing.)
# f1 = fill, f2 = told
# RUN(READ): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(READ): as-written
# READ: PropGet {{*}} key="TEXT"
# READ-NOT: GetSlot
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = () => {};
# ANSWERS: 1 20 300 4000
